# EMDR — marketing: don’t explain in text

On **marketing** surfaces (`.frontend-home`, `app/components/frontend/**`, public `/`, `/about`, `/emdr`, `/learn`, `/blog`, pricing/FAQ sections on the landing), **do not use body copy to explain the product**. Hierarchy, layout, labels, and visuals carry meaning; paragraphs that “teach” are banned unless the surface is explicitly long-form (blog article, editorial, legal).

Still run **redpen** + **writing-copy** + **frontend-design** per `page-copy-design-review.mdc`. Obey **nura-brand** (no BLS jargon, AI agent-guided / Self-guided language, no “moving ball” as the product).

## Use instead of explanatory text

| Job | Use |
|---|---|
| What it is | **Kicker + title** (one idea each) |
| How it feels | **Visual** (mockup, card, icon row, motion) |
| What you get | **Short label** on a card/chip (3–6 words) |
| Next step | **CTA** that says what happens (“Get started”, “See pricing”) |
| Trust / legal | **One line** disclaimer where required — not a paragraph essay |

## Do not

- Stack **title + lead + bullet essay** that all say the same thing
- Write “how it works” prose under a section that already has steps or cards
- Add a second sentence to a hero lead “for clarity” — tighten the title or fix the layout
- Use marketing body text to define Guided vs Free — name modes once in a **labeled card**, not a paragraph
- Explain passkeys, billing, or settings on the landing — that belongs in product/auth microcopy or help

## OK (not “marketing explain”)

- **Blog / editorial / `/emdr` guides** — educational by intent; still no BLS acronym to users
- **FAQ answers** — one short direct answer per question (not section intros)
- **Meta descriptions / JSON-LD** — SEO, not on-page teaching
- **Product / auth / onboarding** — microcopy and forms (`/app`, `.auth-shell`); different rule set (`product-ui`, turnstile)

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — paragraph explains what the section title already claims
<h2>AI agent-guided sessions</h2>
<p>
  Our AI agent walks you through EMDR phases step by step so you always know
  what to do next. You can chat, run visual sets, and track progress in one calm app.
</p>

// ✅ GOOD — title + labeled cards + CTA
<p className="fe-section-kicker">Session modes</p>
<h2 className="fe-section-title">Choose how you practice</h2>
{/* two cards: AI agent-guided · Self-guided session — 1 line each, no essay */}
<Link href="/app/create-account" className="fe-btn-primary">Get started</Link>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — auth-style helper on marketing hero
<p>EMDR therapy online in a calm app with visual sets and optional voice guidance…</p>

// ✅ GOOD — hero title + italic tagline + single CTA (details in product)
<h1>EMDR therapy online. <em>in a calm app.</em></h1>
<Link href="/app/create-account">Get started</Link>
```

## Pass check (marketing only)

- [ ] Removing all `.fe-section-lead` / body paragraphs still leaves the section understandable
- [ ] No block exists only to “explain” what a card, screenshot, or label already shows
- [ ] Kicker, title, and CTA are not three versions of the same sentence
